  "merits": "Salawat & litanies: These are as quoted from Misbah al-Mutahajjid.\n\nSalawat of the Awsiya (recited 10 times): This invocation of God’s blessings upon the Holy Prophet and his Household has been also reported to be said on Fridays with a great reward.\n\nEach of the six phrases 100 times: Every hardship that afflicts you in this world will be made easy with the help of Allah, and He shall make light your burden on the day of judgment. You will remain safe from the oppression of the tyrants. Your belief in Allah shall not weaken in whatever manner Satan tries to lure you to the life of sin.\n\nDua Ya Malik al-Riqab: Imam Hasan bin Ali al-Askari (a.s.) advised the faithful to pray this dua’ after Fajr salaat.\n\nForgiveness for believers: This dua’ is known as the dua’ of Imam Ja’far bin Mohammed al-Sadiq [a.s.].\n\nDua La Ilaha Illallah al-Jalil: Zayn al-Muttaqin says that this multipurpose dua’ was brought by Jibraeel (a.s.) to the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and said: Whoever prays it after Fajr salaat and also keeps it on the body as ta’weez receive the following benefits: Protection from death by accident; Exemption from the questioning by munkar and nakir in the grave; Relief from the fright of abandonment and melancholy in the grave; Diseases will be cured; Safety from oppression and exploitation; The eight gates of heaven will be thrown open for those who pray this dua’."
